  "details": "Like most VRC players, I've had to use the vote kick feature a lot, and too many times has it failed due to other players not knowing what the reason for the kick is. So, I thought of a way to inform everyone of the reason for calling a vote kick on a player.\n\nWhen selecting the vote kick option, another window would appear with a chatbox for typing in the specific reason OR premade options such as \"Cheating\", \"Idle/AFK\", \"Trolling\" (Trolling can have multiple reasons like holding a game hostage or just being a nuisance all together, etc).\n\nAs for the chatbox option, the user can be more specific in what the person is doing, such as \"He/she is being extremely rude to everyone AND using a client\". And if the person calling the votekick uses bad words like slurs and such, it could have a system to filter out those words or just not allow the user to submit the vote to kick due to offensive language being used.",
